# Adapter Pattern

## Rule
UI and domain never import plugin packages directly. Define a narrow interface; implement one adapter per vendor/SDK.

```dart
// domain or core contract
abstract interface class MediaPlayerController {
  Future<void> play(Uri streamUri);
  Future<void> pause();
  Stream<PlayerStatus> get status;
}

// data/adapters — only place that may import the SDK (after approval)
class Media3PlayerAdapter implements MediaPlayerController { ... }
```

## Required adapter families (MVP)
- **Catalog/Sources:** `M3uSourceAdapter`, `XtreamSourceAdapter`, `ProprietaryCatalogAdapter` → canonical `ContentItem` / `Channel`.
- **Playback:** `MediaPlayerController` impl (Media3/ExoPlayer or approved engine).
- **Secure storage / HTTP / WebSocket:** one adapter each; swappable for tests.

## Keep adapters thin
Map types, translate errors to domain `Failure`s, no business rules. No package installs without user approval.
